.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.TH speedqx 1  "speedqx 4.0.0"
.SH NAME
speedqx \- SpeedQX Internet Speed Test \- QubeTX Developer Tools
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBspeedqx\fR [\fB\-\-deep\fR] [\fB\-\-max\-bytes\fR] [\fB\-\-accept\-mlab\fR] [\fB\-\-json\fR] [\fB\-\-ascii\fR] [\fB\-\-no\-color\fR] [\fB\-\-duration\fR] [\fB\-\-fastcom\-duration\fR] [\fB\-\-latency\-probes\fR] [\fB\-\-fast\fR] [\fB\-\-skip\-msak\fR] [\fB\-\-skip\-apple\fR] [\fB\-\-update\fR] [\fB\-v\fR|\fB\-\-version\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] [\fIsubcommands\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
SpeedQX Internet Speed Test \- QubeTX Developer Tools
.PP
Sustained application throughput on this device and path (Methodology v5). Quick is the default, capped at 90 seconds. \-\-deep repeats the primary measurement and adds supplementary sources within five minutes. Cloudflare and M\-Lab MSAK each get one primary vote; NDT7 is a separate single\-stream comparison. M\-Lab requires \-\-accept\-mlab because it publishes measurement results and IP addresses.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-deep\fR
Deep measurement (five\-minute cap; Quick is the default)
.TP
\fB\-\-max\-bytes\fR \fI<MAX_BYTES>\fR
Synthetic payload budget in bytes (default: Quick 5 GB, Deep 20 GB)
.TP
\fB\-\-accept\-mlab\fR
Allow M\-Lab tests: M\-Lab publishes measurement results and your IP address
.TP
\fB\-v\fR, \fB\-\-version\fR
Print version
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
.SH OUTPUT
.TP
\fB\-\-json\fR
Output results as JSON
.TP
\fB\-\-ascii\fR
Use ASCII characters instead of Unicode box\-drawing
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-color\fR
Disable colored output
.SH "SPEED TEST"
.TP
\fB\-\-duration\fR \fI<DURATION>\fR [default: 30]
Legacy duration alias; v5 uses bounded Quick/Deep schedules
.TP
\fB\-\-fastcom\-duration\fR \fI<FASTCOM_DURATION>\fR [default: auto]
Legacy fast.com duration alias; v5 uses a bounded supplementary schedule
.TP
\fB\-\-latency\-probes\fR \fI<LATENCY_PROBES>\fR [default: 20]
Legacy probe\-count alias; v5 uses 12 idle probes
.TP
\fB\-\-fast\fR
Alias for Quick, the default 90\-second profile
.TP
\fB\-\-skip\-msak\fR
Skip the M\-Lab MSAK multi\-stream provider
.TP
\fB\-\-skip\-apple\fR
Legacy alias; Apple networkQuality is outside the common v5 profile
.SH ACTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-update\fR
Check for updates and install the latest version (legacy flag form of `speedqx update`)
.SH SUBCOMMANDS
.TP
speedqx\-update(1)
Check for updates and install the latest release
.TP
speedqx\-help(1)
Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)
.SH EXTRA
EXAMPLES:
  speedqx                          Quick test
  speedqx \-\-accept\-mlab            Quick with both primary networks
  speedqx \-\-deep \-\-accept\-mlab     Deep, five\-minute cap
  speedqx \-\-max\-bytes 250000000    Limit synthetic payload to 250 MB
  speedqx \-\-json                  Machine\-readable results and raw traces
  speedqx update                  Update both CLI tools

\-\-fast remains a Quick alias. Legacy duration and latency\-count flags parse for compatibility; v5 schedules are fixed. Ctrl\-C preserves valid partial results. Payload budgets exclude protocol overhead and may have in\-flight WebSocket overshoot.
